content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Coordinates incident responses and assigns officers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Citizen Report",
      "description": "Initial report submitted by a citizen about an incident."
    },
    {
      "name": "Citizen",
      "description": "Individual reporting an incident to the police department."
    },
    {
      "name": "Incident System",
      "description": "Digital system where incidents are logged and tracked.",
      "attributes": [
        "Incident"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Incident",
      "description": "Recorded event requiring police response.",
      "attributes": [
        "Status",
        "Field Report"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Status",
      "description": "Current state of an incident, such as 'reported', 'in progress', or 'resolved'."
    },
    {
      "name": "Field Report",
      "description": "Summary written by a patrol officer after responding to an incident."
    },
    {
      "name": "Investigation",
      "description": "Ongoing process of examining an incident and collecting evidence.",
      "attributes": [
        "Case File",
        "Incident",
        "Evidence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Case File",
      "description": "Complete record of an investigation, containing all related information."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence",
      "description": "Physical or digital material collected for an investigation."
    },
    {
      "name": "Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Responds to reported incidents and files field reports."
    },
    {
      "name": "Case Transfer",
      "description": "Formal process of assigning a case from a patrol officer to an investigator.",
      "attributes": [
        "Incident"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Investigator",
      "description": "Handles complex cases and leads investigations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Request",
      "description": "Request sent by an investigator for evidence collection or analysis."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Technician",
      "description": "Collects, logs, and manages physical evidence."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Database",
      "description": "System for recording and storing details of collected evidence.",
      "attributes": [
        "Evidence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Records Clerk",
      "description": "Archives completed case files in the department’s record system."
    },
    {
      "name": "Record System",
      "description": "Central archive for managing and retrieving case files.",
      "attributes": [
        "Case File"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Investigation": {
      "objects": [
        "Investigator",
        "Investigation",
        "Case File"
      ]
    },
    "First Response": {
      "objects": [
        "Patrol Officer",
        "Incident",
        "Field Report",
        "Case Transfer"
      ]
    },
    "Record Keeping": {
      "objects": [
        "Records Clerk",
        "Record System",
        "Case File"
      ]
    },
    "Dispatch": {
      "objects": [
        "Citizen",
        "Citizen Report",
        "Dispatcher",
        "Incident System",
        "Incident",
        "Status"
      ]
    },
    "Forensics": {
      "objects": [
        "Evidence Request",
        "Evidence Technician",
        "Evidence Database",
        "Evidence"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Investigation Operations": {
      "derived from": [
        "Investigation Subdomain",
        "Forensics Subdomain"
      ],
      "objects": [
        "Investigator",
        "Investigation",
        "Case Documentation",
        "Evidence Request",
        "Evidence Technician",
        "Evidence Database",
        "Evidence"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Case File -> Case Documentation"
      ]
    },
    "First Response": {
      "derived from": "First Response Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Patrol Officer",
        "Incident",
        "Field Report",
        "Case Transfer"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Incident -> Incident Response"
      ]
    },
    "Record Keeping": {
      "derived from": "Record Keeping Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Records Clerk",
        "Record System",
        "Closed Case"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Case File -> Closed Case"
      ]
    },
    "Dispatch": {
      "derived from": "Dispatch Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Citizen",
        "Citizen Report",
        "Dispatcher",
        "Incident System",
        "Incident",
        "Status"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    }
  }
}
```
